reframe:
SSBench cites tiny MDPs even for large cores. A big reason for this is likely the requirement of many MDP read ports to avoid stalling dispatch, for instance XiangShan has 8 read ports. Power and iso-comparisons are also big reasons on small cores. This suggests the perforamnce delivered by 128 SSIT entries with XS Store Sets is actually very realistic, and a generous estimation to the baseline storage budget for area-constrained cores. We evaluate small *and* medium with 128 SSIT entries. While there are potential hardware solutions to this problem (constable, renaming, bloom filters), PG-MDP is able to offer these gains without introducing any additional storage or complexity, and without penalties that come from collisions and warmup. 

-MDP constraints (payoff through ILP, high number of read ports, power on small cores)
-128 SSIT entries -> 0.3KB, SSBench suggests 
